 she joins  us live now from Washington DC to talk  more about this thanks very much for  being with us  um now as we were saying these are uh  annual uh drills that uh that NATO and  and the Russians are regularly conduct  but of course they've taken on  um much greater significance with the  war in Ukraine and that's part of the  reason uh we're talking to you just just  talk us through what we should be  looking for here  yes as you say these exercises take  place every year and and unsurprisingly  so because if you've got nuclear weapons  you've got to exercise how you would be  using them uh otherwise you will lose  those skills but obviously what what has  changed in the past six months or so is  Russia's signaling uh or the signaling  by by some Russian officials that Russia  may be willing to use or prepare to use  nuclear weapons against Ukraine and so  uh these exercises that we which you  usually take place without much public  uh interest at all are now suddenly  extremely interesting and and they are  interesting not just for for NATO to  watch what the Russians are doing and  and vice versa but also for the general  public in Ukraine and indeed for all of  us because if a nuclear weapon is used  somewhere  uh it it clearly uh would uh mean risk  escalation that would involve all of us  but we should also remember that that  exercises are merely that it doesn't  mean that that these uh either side is  more or less willing to use in nuclear  weapon but it does come against the  background of Russia being willing to  use nuclear weapons and is there any  significance in these exercises taking  place at the same time  there really isn't it's these sorts of  things uh all military exercises are  scheduled long in advance but I think  what what is really uh crucial to be  watching it this year is what what the  Russians do now they are not very  transparent about their military  exercises ever uh so it's it's not very  easy to discern what exactly they they 